# SRG-APP-000825-AU-000280  -  CAT II
# The Central Log Server must implement multifactor authentication for
# local; network; and/or remote access to privileged accounts; and/or
# nonprivileged accounts such that the device meets organization-defined
# strength of mechanism requirements.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000825-AU-000280
group:           V-263573
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      documented
cci:             CCI-004047
control_rev5:    IA-2

contribution:    The strength of the authenticator device is organization-defined, so the
                 application's share is that it expresses a multifactor mechanism at all
                 and binds it to a user identity. The benchmark authority's implementation
                 for this product (SPLK-CL-000490) is the DoD CAC or other PKI credential,
                 which Splunk expresses through web.conf [settings] enableCertBasedUserAuth
                 plus certBasedUserAuthMethod; the product's alternative is a Duo or RSA
                 vendor named in authentication.conf [authentication]
                 externalTwoFactorAuthVendor/externalTwoFactorAuthSettings.

governs:         web.conf - Configures the Splunk Web interface.

check:           web.conf [settings] enableCertBasedUserAuth in true|True|TRUE|t|1|yes
check:           web.conf [settings] certBasedUserAuthMethod in CommonName|EDIPI|PIV
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          web.conf [settings] certBasedUserAuthMethod https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/manage-users-and-security/10.4/authenticate-into-splunk-enterprise-using-hardware/configure-splunk-enterprise-to-use-a-common-access-card-for-authentication
vendor:          web.conf [settings] enableCertBasedUserAuth https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/manage-users-and-security/10.4/authenticate-into-splunk-enterprise-using-hardware/configure-splunk-enterprise-to-use-a-common-access-card-for-authentication
# --- end vendor verification

external:        The strength-of-mechanism requirement itself - organization-defined; no
                 product setting states or measures a device's assurance level, so the
                 criterion asserts only that a mechanism is configured.
external:        The assurance level of the CAC/PIV token or of the Duo/RSA device -
                 carried by the DoD PKI or the multifactor vendor.
external:        Where the configured path is the product's native Duo or RSA integration
                 rather than certificates, the factor is carried by authentication.conf
                 externalTwoFactorAuthVendor/externalTwoFactorAuthSettings (also observed
                 on this requirement) and the certificate settings may legitimately be
                 absent.
external:        Where PKI is terminated by an approved SSO proxy per SPLK-CL-000490, the
                 mechanism is carried by that proxy.

citation:        splunk-spec-files/web.conf.spec:120, :133;
                 splunk-spec-files/authentication.conf.spec:87, :95; SPLK-CL-000490 check
                 and fix text
finding:         No multifactor mechanism is configured in the application -
                 certificate-based user authentication is off in web.conf [settings] and no
                 Duo or RSA vendor is named in authentication.conf [authentication], so no
                 device of any strength is required at login; this determination is from
                 the perspective of the application layer alone, the strength-of-mechanism
                 value being organization-defined and the device supplied outside the
                 application.
